       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The maximum labeled dose is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single 1,700 mg dose is also above the usual per-dose maximum of 1,000 mg. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals\n- Another dose\n\nTell me the dose you intend and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it."
